          ],
          "content": "PAIR OF LINEAR EQUATIONS IN TWO VARIABLES"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.104,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "33"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.139,
            0.139,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "i.e.,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.404,
            0.138,
            0.514,
            0.157
          ],
          "content": "8 - 12 = 0",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.161,
            0.515,
            0.179
          ],
          "content": "i.e., – 4 = 0"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.186,
            0.358,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": "which is a false statement."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.208,
            0.902,
            0.247
          ],
          "content": "Therefore, the equations do not have a common solution. $\\mathrm { S o } ,$ the two rails will not cross each other."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.409,
            0.28,
            0.591,
            0.299
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "EXERCISE 3.2"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.31,
            0.778,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": "**1.** Solve the following pair of linear equations by the substitution method."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.333,
            0.651,
            0.352
          ],
          "content": "(i) $x + y = 1 4$ (ii) $s - t   =   3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.202,
            0.372,
            0.285,
            0.389
          ],
          "content": "x   -   y   =   4",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.576,
            0.362,
            0.675,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "{ \\frac { s } { 3 } } + { \\frac { t } { 2 } } = 6",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_11.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.162,
            0.401,
            0.302,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": "(iii) $3 x   -   y   =   3$ $9x - 3y = 9$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.536,
            0.401,
            0.715,
            0.419
          ],
          "continues_prev": true,
          "content": "(iv) $0.2x + 0.3y = 1.3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.572,
            0.419,
            0.715,
            0.437
          ],
          "content": "0.4x + 0.5y = 2.3",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.458,
            0.339,
            0.481
          ],
          "content": "(v) $\\sqrt{2} x + \\sqrt{3} y = 0$"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.535,
            0.451,
            0.716,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{3x}{2}-\\frac{5y}{3}=-2",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_16.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.502,
            0.35,
            0.525
          ],
          "content": "\\left\\{ { \\sqrt { 3 } }   x - { \\sqrt { 8 } }   y = 0 \\right.",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.575,
            0.494,
            0.689,
            0.532
          ],
          "content": "\\frac{x}{3} + \\frac{y}{2} = \\frac{13}{6}",
          "image_source": "images/page_9_equation_18.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.536,
            0.9,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "**2.** Solve $2x + 3y = 11$ and $2x - 4y = - 24$ and hence find the value of $\\cdot _ { m ^ { \\prime } }$ for which $y = m x + 3$"
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.563,
            0.983
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.123,
            0.577,
            0.9,
            0.614
          ],
          "content": "**3.** Form the pair of linear equations for the following problems and find their solution by substitution method."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.169,
            0.619,
            0.9,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": "(i) The difference between two numbers is 26 and one number is three times the other. Find them."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.662,
            0.902,
            0.698
          ],
          "content": "(ii) The larger of two supplementary angles exceeds the smaller by 18 degrees. Find them."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.703,
            0.902,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": "(iii) The coach of a cricket team buys 7 bats and 6 balls for \\` 3800. Later, she buys 3 bats and 5 balls for \\` 1750. Find the cost of each bat and each ball."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.16,
            0.745,
            0.903,
            0.832
          ],
          "content": "(iv) The taxi charges in a city consist of a fixed charge together with the charge for the distance covered. For a distance of 10 km, the charge paid is \\` 105 and for a journey of 15 km, the charge paid is \\` 155. What are the fixed charges and the charge per km? How much does a person have to pay for travelling a distance of 25 km?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.831,
            0.902,
            0.897
          ],
          "content": "(v) A fraction becomes $\\frac { 9 } { 1 1 }$ , if 2 is added to both the numerator and the denominator. If, 3 is added to both the numerator and the denominator it becomes $\\frac{5}{6}$ . Find the fraction."
        }
      ]
    }
